All 3 remaining failures are pre-existing in the baseline and unrelated to this fix (they fail identically without my change). The fix resolves the one failing test related to this issue.

**Fix** in `lib/adapters/http.js:280`:

```js
if (config.maxBodyLength > -1) {
  options.maxBodyLength = config.maxBodyLength;
} else {
  // follow-redirects defaults maxBodyLength to 10MB, so we need to
  // disable the limit explicitly if axios maxBodyLength is unlimited (-1)
  options.maxBodyLength = Infinity;
}
```

**Why the bug happened:** axios's default `maxBodyLength` is `-1` (unlimited), so the adapter skipped passing `maxBodyLength` to `follow-redirects`. That library then applied its own default 10MB limit — and inconsistently skipped it when `maxRedirects: 0` used native `http`. Now the adapter explicitly passes `Infinity` to `follow-redirects` when the limit is disabled, making behavior consistent (while an explicit positive `maxBodyLength` is still enforced by both axios and `follow-redirects`).

**Verification:** Full unit suite went from 62 passing / 4 failing (baseline) to 63 passing / 3 failing — the FAIL_TO_PASS test `should properly support default max body length (follow-redirects as well)` now passes and no regressions were introduced.
